7 1 Town or City Clerk; Dog Licenses; Warrants for Nonpayment. Amend RSA 466:14 to read as
8 follows:
9 466:14 Warrants; Proceedings. The town or city clerk shall annually, between June 1 and June
10 20,presenttothelocalgoverningbodyalistofthoseownersofdogsthathavefailedtolicenseornot
11 renewed their dog licenses pursuant to RSA 466:1. The local governing body [shall] may, within 20
12 days from June 20, issue a warrant to a local official authorized to issue a civil forfeiture for each
13 unlicensed dog. The warrant may also authorize a local law enforcement officer to seize any
14 unlicensed dog. The civil forfeiture may be sent by certified mail, or delivered in hand, or left at the
15 abode of the dog owner. The cost of service shall not exceed $7 and may be recovered by the city or
16 town in addition to the amount of the civil forfeiture. If the unlicensed dog is seized, it shall be held
17 inatownorcityholdingfacilityforaperiodof7days,afterwhichtimefulltitletothedogshallpass
18 to the facility, unless the owner of the dog has, before the expiration of the period, caused the dog to
19 be licensed. The owner shall pay the facility a necessary and reasonable sum per day, as agreed
20 upon by the governing body of the town or city and the facility, for each day the dog has been kept
21 and maintained by the facility, plus any necessary veterinary fees incurred by the facility for the
22 benefit of the dog. Before a local law enforcement officer seizes any unlicensed dog, a written
23 warningshallbegiventothedogowner.
24 2 EffectiveDate. Thisactshalltakeeffect60daysafteritspassage.
